4) Install & test in Firefox (temporary add-on)
Open Firefox → go to about:debugging#/runtime/this-firefox
Click “Load Temporary Add-on…”
Select your manifest.json inside chatgpt-export-mvp/
Visit https://chat.openai.com/ and open any conversation
Hover a message: you should see an Export button in/near the native controls
Click it → you’ll get an alert and a console log noting which message you clicked
Tip: Open DevTools (F12) to see the [ChatGPT Export MVP] console logs.
What this MVP proves
Reliable mounting (tries native toolbar first; otherwise overlays cleanly).
Shadow DOM keeps our styles safe from ChatGPT CSS.
MutationObserver ensures buttons appear on newly loaded/streamed messages.
Zero exporting logic yet—just an echo so we can wire actions next.
When you’re ready for Step 2, we’ll wire the click to gather the conversation DOM and serialize to Markdown/HTML/JSON (keeping this mounting approach).

