What you get now
A persistent bottom-right Export button like before.
On click, it:
Scans the page for message containers (robust selector set).
Builds a modular model: conversation meta → messages → segments (text, code, image, table, math).
Saves it at window.__CGPT_EXPORT.lastHarvest.
Logs it to the console.
Tries to copy the JSON to your clipboard (from the click gesture), and shows a quick alert.
This gives us a solid, structured foundation so the next step can be a small in-page UI to filter/toggle/group messages or export in different formats—without redoing the parser.
